Subject: [PATCH 09/17] ttf: a named class's code is its members, without
 brackets

A feature class's code is its member list; the writers add the brackets
(@name = [code];). The reader stored the class with its brackets, so it was
written as @class_0 = [[...]];, which no feature compiler parses: every
font with a context coverage of five glyphs or more failed to build.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
